# 1. Image Commands

👉 docker pull <image>
➡️ Downloads an image from Docker Hub
👉 Example: docker pull nginx

👉 docker images
➡️ Shows all downloaded images

👉 docker rmi <image_id>
➡️ Deletes an image from system

🔹 2. Run Container
👉 docker run <image>
➡️ Runs a container from image

👉 docker run -d <image>
➡️ Runs container in background

👉 docker run -it <image> bash
➡️ Runs container in interactive terminal

👉 docker run --name mycontainer <image>
➡️ Runs container with custom name

# 3. Container Management

👉 docker ps
➡️ Shows running containers

👉 docker ps -a
➡️ Shows all containers (running + stopped)

👉 docker stop <id>
➡️ Stops a running container

👉 docker start <id>
➡️ Starts a stopped container

👉 docker restart <id>
➡️ Restarts container

👉 docker rm <id>
➡️ Deletes a container

# 4. Logs & Info

👉 docker logs <id>
➡️ Shows container output/logs

👉 docker inspect <id>
➡️ Shows detailed info (IP, config, etc.)

👉 docker stats
➡️ Shows CPU & memory usage

🔹 5. Execute Inside Container
👉 docker exec -it <id> bash
➡️ Run commands inside container

🔹 6. Build & Push (Important 🔥)
👉 docker build -t myimage .
➡️ Creates image from Dockerfile

👉 docker tag myimage repo/name
➡️ Tags image for Docker Hub

👉 docker push repo/name
➡️ Uploads image to Docker Hub

🔹 7. Ports
👉 docker run -p 3000:3000 <image>
➡️ Connects container port to local machine

🔹 8. Volumes
👉 docker volume create myvolume
➡️ Creates storage volume

👉 docker run -v myvolume:/data <image>
➡️ Mounts volume to container

🔹 9. Docker Compose
👉 docker-compose up
➡️ Starts multiple containers

👉 docker-compose down
➡️ Stops all containers


🔥 Super Important (Interview Focus)
commands:
docker pull → download
docker run → run container
docker ps → check running
docker build → create image
docker exec → access container

🚀 One-line Summary 
Docker commands help to create, run, manage, and deploy containers efficiently.

# 🐳 Docker Commands
🟢 1. docker pull IMAGE_NAME:version
📖 Meaning
👉 Downloads image from Docker registry (Docker Hub)

🧠 Example
docker pull nginx:latest
👉 Downloads nginx image

🟢 2. docker run -d IMAGE_NAME
📖 Meaning
👉 Runs a container in detached mode (background)

🧠 Example
docker run -d nginx
👉 Container runs in background

🟢 3. docker run --name CONT_NAME -d IMAGE_NAME
📖 Meaning
👉 Runs container with a custom name

🧠 Example
docker run --name mynginx -d nginx
👉 Container name = mynginx

🎯 Quick Revision
pull → download image
run -d → run in background
--name → give custom name


# Docker — Troubleshoot Commands
🟢 1. docker logs CONT_ID
📖 Meaning
👉 Shows logs/output of a container
🧠 Use
Check errors
Debug issues
🧾 Example
docker logs mycontainer

🟢 2. docker exec -it CONT_ID /bin/bash
📖 Meaning
👉 Open interactive terminal (bash) inside container

🧠 Use
Debug inside container
Check files, run commands
🧾 Example
docker exec -it mycontainer /bin/bash

🟢 3. docker exec -it CONT_ID /bin/sh
📖 Meaning
👉 Open sh shell (lightweight terminal)

🧠 Use
When bash is not available
Minimal containers (like Alpine)
🧾 Example
docker exec -it mycontainer /bin/sh

🎯 Quick Difference
logs → view output
exec bash → full terminal
exec sh → basic terminal



